; The retain/release protocol: Rust holding an Axiom value past a call.
;
; Rust may NOT keep an Axiom heap value beyond the shim that received
; it. The borrow is the call - ARC may release the block the moment the
; call returns, and an arena reset may reclaim it wholesale. A shim that
; wants to keep one takes a share with `axiom_retain` and pairs it with
; `axiom_release`, both of which have external linkage in every emitted
; module.
;
; `axffi_str_keep` retains, stashes, and answers the length; `axffi_str_recall`
; reads the stashed value back; `axffi_str_drop` releases. This case
; churns 500 strings through that cycle, so a missing retain shows up as
; a wrong length or a crash rather than as luck.
;
; A literal's count word is -1 - the statics sentinel - so retaining one
; is free and releasing one is a no-op. The strings here are BUILT, not
; literal, so they are counted blocks and the protocol is real.
;
; `(cast Foreign s)` is the documented escape, and it is the honest
; spelling: retain and release operate on a WORD, not on a `String`.
; The declaration in `Demo.ax` says `Foreign` for exactly that reason.
(import IO)

(import Fmt)

(import Str)

(import Demo)

(pub :: churn (-> Int Int Int))

(pub fn (churn i acc)
  (if (>= i 500)
    acc
    (let ((s (strConcat "abc" "de")))
      (let ((n 
        (strKeep
          (cast Foreign s)
        )
      ))
        (let ((back strRecall))
          {
            strDrop
            (churn
              (+ i 1)              (+
                acc                (if (== back n)
                  1
                  0
                )
              )
            )
          }
        )
      )
    )
  )
)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(pub fn (main)
  (let ((ok (churn 0 0)))
    (if (== ok 500)
      {
        (println "arc retain: agree")
        0
      }
      {
        (println (fmtInt ok))
        1
      }
    )
  )
)
; expect 0
